matrix-overlay (0.1.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Store metadata now survives AppStream processing: the icon SVG parses under
    gdk-pixbuf (no comments before the root element), media URLs no longer rely
    on redirects, and the component category is one AppStream accepts. Broken
    any of these, and appstream-compose drops the component from the catalogue
    without saying so.
  * Published as a signed apt repository (packaging/publish_repo.sh): the
    repository now ships the DEP-11 catalogue with a Package link, so COSMIC
    Store can install the app rather than merely describe it.
  * Documentation: the packaging rules that were measured on a client (catalogue
    path, three compressed forms, Origin header, Package link), the render-node
    selection ladder, and why the store route is native and not Flatpak.

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:12:00 +0200

matrix-overlay (0.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release: GPU-composited Matrix rain over every output on
    COSMIC/Wayland, triggered by a custom shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+M by convention).
  * The render node and EGL vendor are detected from the connectors that are
    actually driven, so one package serves hybrid and single-GPU machines.
  * Config chain: --config, MATRIX_OVERLAY_CONFIG, ~/.config, then
    /etc/matrix-overlay/config.toml (installed here as a conffile).
  * Cairo/GTK layer-shell painting remains as a fallback for compositors whose
    GL path is unusable; it is a Recommends, not a Depends.

 -- Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:19:48 +0200
